@startuml
title Milestone 3B - errors, correction and reconciliation
actor "Estate manager" as M
participant Operations as O
database "Operations DB" as D
participant "Confirmed outbox relay" as R
queue RabbitMQ as Q
participant "Future consumer (not implemented)" as C
M -> O : correction / void; reason + version + Idempotency-Key
O -> O : current role/estate authorization; receipt check
alt invalid input / unauthorized / stale
 O --> M : 400 / 403 / 409 ProblemDetail + correlation
 note over O,D : No committed mutation, history, command reservation or event.
else valid new command
 O -> D : BEGIN; reserve key; conditional root update
 O -> D : before/after revision + adjustment + full snapshot event + receipt
 alt persistence / serialization failure
  O -> D : ROLLBACK all writes
  O --> M : sanitized failure; retry same key
 else committed
  O -> D : COMMIT
  O --> M : 200 applied manager action
 end
end
R -> D : lock committed due outbox row
R -> Q : same stable eventId on every attempt
alt confirm positive and no mandatory return
 Q --> R : ack
 R -> D : mark PUBLISHED and commit
else nack / return / timeout / outage
 R -> D : capped backoff; finite attempts; retain FAILED
 note over R,D : Repair cause then operator resets selected IDs, never regenerates.
end
Q -> C : duplicate or out-of-order full snapshots
C -> C : future atomic eventId dedup + highest version
C -> C : replace prior contribution; VOIDED tombstone contributes zero
note over D,C
Reconcile latest root/revision/outbox aggregate version.
Later date correction reverses consumer's old grouping contribution.
History retains original observed evidence.
end note
@enduml
